  "notes": "USAGE:\nMost commonly used with する to form a verb meaning \"to start up\" or \"to boot.\" Frequently appears in computing contexts but also applies to machines, engines, and systems in general.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- パソコンを{起動|きどう}する (to start up a computer)\n- アプリを{起動|きどう}する (to launch an app)\n- {起動|きどう}が{遅|おそ}い (slow to start)\n- {起動|きどう}{時|じ} (at startup)\n- {再|さい}{起動|きどう}する (to restart)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {軌道|きどう}: orbit; track — a homophone with a completely different meaning\n- {起動|きどう} vs {再|さい}{起動|きどう}: {起動|きどう} is initial startup, while {再起動|さいきどう} is restarting",
